      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Biological membranes separate the cells from the environment and control flow of molecules and information between the cell and its surroundings. In addition, the cellular energy supply is dependent on membrane functions. The present chapter deals with membrane lipid peroxidation and how this process might influence the physiology and pathophysiology of the myocardium."},
